commits.message:
docs: credit everyone who touched the header and auth surface

#92 is the one that matters: @GhimBoon pasted `Headers: (none)` under an
explicit --header argument and concluded the headers were dropped. That
conclusion was reasonable because the gateway said so, and GW-006 is
exactly why it said so. @ArnaudBger, @alvaroalon2 and others carried that
thread.

@bbracha-evinced was debugging --oauth2Bearer with the same startup log as
their first diagnostic. @homer6 filed the repo's earlier note about not
leaking a token through a side channel, which is the class GW-029 belongs
to. @akirilyuk ships these logs to a central store, which is where the
token was going. @iutx asked for bearer auth in the first place;
@davidferlay was on that thread. @bossanyit, @thedadams, @gamedevsam and
@hxy91819 worked the header and auth surface this change touches.

docs: credit the #18 reporters behind SSE client isolation

@tttcoding666 reported #18: with several SSE clients connected, every
client received every other client's messages. @aneasystone and
@luyunfeng-bytedance confirmed it on that thread. #221 fixes it by giving
each SSE connection its own child, so replies reach only the session that
made the request.
